+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2G2AGPX8KWSY1KXGYADK4TK","supersedes":"fnd_01M2G2AGPX8KWSY1KXGYADK4TK","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"find/export tools return full unmasked documents from pii/financial-classified collections","description":"FindTool.execute (find.ts:108-118) returns cursorResults.documents serialised via EJSON.stringify() verbatim inside the tool's untrusted-data content, with no field projection enforcement, masking or x-data-classification annotation (the caller-supplied `projection` argument is optional and not required). ExportTool (export.ts) writes complete find/aggregate result sets to a file exposed via resource URI or local path (isServerRunningLocally branch). No schema under src/tools/mongodb carries any masking metadata. mcp-gateway's qa and prod MongoDB stores are classified [pii, financial] (env/qa.json, env/prod.json) and the README names them client-data and order stores. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.DS.S4. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (The cited evidence supports the claim: find.ts:108-118 returns cursorResults.documents through EJSON.stringify inside formatUntrustedData with an optional passthrough projection and no masking; export.ts sends whole find/aggregate cursors to createJSONExport and adds the local-path branch; src/tools/mongodb has no mask, redact or classification code (the only redact calls, in tool.ts and telemetry, clean secrets out of error and telemetry text, not document fields); the deploy overlays only disable atlas-local, so find and export stay reachable; env/qa.json and env/prod.json classify the data as [pii, financial] (prod exposure partner); the README names the client-data and order stores; the SARIF export (session 2853edbc) holds an SCH-API-03 fail result at src/tools/mongodb/read/find.ts:108-118 with the same fingerprint and control ids; and high equals the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.DS.S4 (the SARIF rule has no security-severity). Minor cleanups (not refuting): evidence[0] and evidence[2] are the same SARIF export and should be merged into one entry with the sha256, and env/qa.json and env/prod.json are cited in the description but missing from evidence[]. Unverifiable: the export sha256 cannot be recomputed here; it matches only the sarifSha256 the caller supplied.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (Under the regulatory-mapping lens the refs hold up: SEBI is cited first for this mid-size stock broker, the CSCRF catalog's PR.DS.S4 does cover how web applications handle PII and business data, and severity high matches PR.DS.S4's defaultSeverity because the SARIF rule has no security-severity score; one caveat is that DPDP Rule 6 does not take effect until 2027-05-13 (instruments.json structure), so 6(1)(a) is a forward-looking second ref, not a clause that binds today; also, the description's 'SLA topic: patch-sla' fits a missing masking feature poorly and may belong to the defaults row instead, but slaBasis was outside this check (unverifiable: OWASP ASVS 5.0 14.2.6 has no catalog in the workspace, so its id and text were not confirmed).).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S4","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(a)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.DS.S4"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(a)"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-asvs-5.0","controlId":"14.2.6"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/tools/mongodb/read/find.ts","startLine":108,"endLine":118},"fingerprint":"a051281ec7c4f32cd9052b215ce8f8af38130ca5fb16387613ceeba362a41f5e","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"SCH-API-03","tool":"maxwell-schema-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","initiativeId":"init_01M2GWJSJ3JACXRBXFT116SPFH","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13: