+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GMWQ01QA647X5MYFGNS1MG","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"MDB_MCP_DRY_RUN dumps the full resolved config, including isSecret-marked fields, with no redaction","description":"DryRunModeRunner.dumpConfig() (src/transports/dryModeRunner.ts:43-46) runs `this.consoleLogger.log(JSON.stringify(this.userConfig, null, 2))`, printing the entire resolved UserConfig object to stdout, including connectionString, apiClientId, apiClientSecret and voyageApiKey -- every one of which userConfig.ts marks isSecret:true -- with no call to the mongodb-redact `redact()` helper that every other logging path in this codebase uses (LoggerBase.redactIfNecessary, loggerBase.ts:42-67; Telemetry.sendEvents, telemetry.ts:339-363). server.json documents --dryRun/MDB_MCP_DRY_RUN as a supported operator flag ('dumps configuration and enabled tools, then exits without starting the server'), so this is a reachable, documented code path, not a test-only helper. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S1. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (The claim holds. dryModeRunner.ts:43-46 runs console.log on JSON.stringify(this.userConfig) with no redact() call. TransportRunnerBase stores the userConfig object unchanged (base.ts:238), and index.ts:187-199 passes a plain console logger, so nothing redacts it on the way out. userConfig.ts marks connectionString, apiClientId, apiClientSecret (30-46) and voyageApiKey (211-217) isSecret:true. The cited redaction paths are real: loggerBase.ts:42-67 and telemetry.ts:339-363, with redact() at lines 347-348. server.json:332-333 documents --dryRun. The SARIF export contains a matching SCH-API-06 fail result at the same path and lines, with maxwell/v1 equal to the candidate fingerprint. Severity high equals the PR.AA.S1 catalog defaultSeverity and cannot be lowered under the severity rule. Two caveats, neither a reason to refute: (1) no deploy manifest (deploy/aws, deploy/azure) or env record sets MDB_MCP_DRY_RUN, so the leak needs an operator to run the flag, and the output would then reach stdout and container logs (prod logs are kept 365 days in Wazuh), not a remote attacker; (2) 'every other logging path uses redact()' overstates slightly, because the help/version handlers also call console.log directly, though they print no config. Unverifiable: the export sha256 ac53f2a6... cannot be recomputed here.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The mapping can be fixed, so this is not refuted: the regulators match, the instruments apply, both control ids exist in the catalogs and ledger, SEBI is correctly cited first, and severity high is PR.AA.S1's catalog default (no CVSS), but DPDP 6(1)(a) covers encrypting or masking personal data while the leaked fields are credentials, so 6(1)(b) (access control over computer resources, also high, ledger record present) fits better. Details: sebi-cscrf-2024 and dpdp-rules-2025 are in frameworksInScope and cover stock-broker/DP/nbfc; the category mid-size-re is listed; example-co has 5 ledger lines for PR.AA.S1 and 2 for 6(1)(a). PR.AA.S1 is about issuing, managing, verifying, revoking and auditing credentials, so dumping isSecret credentials to stdout is a fair match. Swapping in 6(1)(b) does not change severity. Minor notes: (1) PR.AA.S1 probeWorkflows do not include probe-schemas; (2) the registry lists DPDP Rule 6 in force only from 2027-05-13, after NOW (2026-09-14), so it binds only through the company's own scoping; (3) the company is also an nbfc-middle-layer with rbi-cyber-tech-directions-2026 in scope and no RBI ref is cited, so an RBI credential-management paragraph could be added second; (4) the description names patch-sla as the topic, but PR.AA.S1 has no patch-sla row, so the SEBI patch row cannot be matched directly (slaBasis is left to the ledger keeper). (unverifiable: OWASP ASVS 5.0 13.3.1 wording, since the workspace has no ASVS catalog; 16.2.5, not logging credentials, may fit better.)).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S1","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(b)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S1"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(b)"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-asvs-5.0","controlId":"13.3.1"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/transports/dryModeRunner.ts","startLine":43,"endLine":46},"fingerprint":"49267cdf1a324766f10abeb9c77a8013f739246a1da95044d1dc7ead56dad469","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"SCH-API-06","tool":"maxwell-schema-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T18:36:43Z","relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GMWPY9B54SGT32H9MFQ5KY","obs_01M2GMWPSGBCYNXA6S2ZR7ZT5R"],"evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/2853edbc-3a09-4ec1-87ad-1afe187bb68c/probe-schemas.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"ac53f2a64f99af00b6ec6e40eb92f649a78ae68fbe90db7cc9f36ffe8a5c4e6c","description":"SCH-API-06 result (dryModeRunner.ts)"}],"tags":["schema","data-protection","static-probe","secrets","dry-run"],"provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-9948-b23539a1495a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"},"supersedes":"fnd_01M2GMWQ01QA647X5MYFGNS1MG","initiativeId":"init_01M2GWKQNTJ7082K1R20CDEN2P"}
