+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2G2AGVRZPBP3VH8FNAYH46V","supersedes":"fnd_01M2G2AGVRZPBP3VH8FNAYH46V","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"mcp-gateway's HTTP transport (/mcp) has no default authentication","description":"src/transports/mcpHttpServer.ts setupMiddlewares() (lines 306-319) is the only gate on the /mcp POST/GET/DELETE routes (lines 360-411), which reach every registered MongoDB and Atlas tool including insert-many, delete-many, drop-collection, drop-database and connect. It loops over userConfig.httpHeaders and rejects a request only when a configured header/value pair is missing; httpHeaders defaults to {} (src/common/config/userConfig.ts:136-143, overrideBehavior 'not-allowed') and server.json documents --httpHeaders/MDB_MCP_HTTP_HEADERS as an optional, non-secret setting. With no operator configuration, every /mcp request is served with zero authentication. streamableHttp.ts (shouldWarnAboutHttpHost) only logs a warning when httpHost is non-loopback; it enforces nothing. mcp-gateway's qa and prod environments run this server on EKS ap-south-1 with dataClassification [pii, financial]; prod exposure is 'partner'. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S17. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (Every cited fact is in the files: mcpHttpServer.ts 306-319 checks only userConfig.httpHeaders and /mcp POST/GET/DELETE are at 360-411; userConfig.ts 136-143 defaults httpHeaders to {} with overrideBehavior not-allowed; server.json marks MDB_MCP_HTTP_HEADERS and --httpHeaders isRequired false and isSecret false; shouldWarnAboutHttpHost only logs; the tools insert-many, delete-many, drop-collection, drop-database and connect exist; nothing else in src/transports does auth; the in-repo deploy files add none for EKS (the AWS Dockerfile binds 0.0.0.0 with no headers, its bearer token belongs to Bedrock AgentCore, and Azure defaults to NOAUTH); prod.json shows partner exposure and [pii, financial], qa.json shows qa on EKS ap-south-1 with the same classification; the SARIF export has a SCH-API-01 fail result at the same path and lines with maxwell/v1 fingerprint equal to the candidate's; high matches the PR.AA.S17 catalog defaultSeverity. Style only: evidence[0] and evidence[2] both point at the same SARIF export and should be one entry carrying the sha256. (unverifiable: the SARIF sha256 cannot be computed here, but it matches the context sarifSha256; no EKS manifests or values in the workspace show whether prod sets httpHeaders or has an ingress/mesh auth layer, and the finding is correctly framed as a code-default gap.)); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The mapping holds: sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S17 (API authentication, authorisation and access management so only intended entities reach APIs) and dpdp-rules-2025 6(1)(b) (access control on computer resources) both exist in their catalogs, both are in example-co's frameworksInScope, and PR.AA.S17's reCategories cover the company's active mid-size-re SEBI registrations. Both control records exist in the ledger, and prod.json confirms the pii data classification, so the DPDP ref applies. SEBI is cited first as the most specific Indian instrument, since the app supports order routing for the broker. The SARIF export has no security-severity or CVSS score, so severity high correctly comes from PR.AA.S17's catalog defaultSeverity (high). Non-blocking note: the global ref owasp-asvs-5.0 8.2.1 is not among PR.AA.S17's catalog mappings (the catalog maps ASVS V4, plus nist-csf-2.0 PR.AA-05 and cis-controls-8.1 16.13), and there is no ASVS catalog to check the 8.2.1 wording against. It is a secondary ref from an instrument that applies to everyone, so it does not refute. Optional: company is also an RBI NBFC with rbi-cyber-tech-directions-2026 in scope, so an RBI access-control clause could be added as a secondary ref (unverifiable: ASVS 5.0 8.2.1 text).).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S17","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(b)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S17"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(b)"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-asvs-5.0","controlId":"8.2.1"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/transports/mcpHttpServer.ts","startLine":306,"endLine":319},"fingerprint":"2b47a8fb3b6e3225e8b94541ffb4b7c068f7cb9440d9d22aa3c053fe690a20a6","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"SCH-API-01","tool":"maxwell-schema-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:14:50Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T13:14:50Z","relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GMWPRJJM5QFJX3G6NBT6JR","obs_01M2GMWPSGBCYNXA6S2ZR7ZT5R"],"evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/2853edbc-3a09-4ec1-87ad-1afe187bb68c/probe-schemas.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"ac53f2a64f99af00b6ec6e40eb92f649a78ae68fbe90db7cc9f36ffe8a5c4e6c","description":"SCH-API-01 result"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json","description":"exposure: partner, dataClassification: [pii, financial]"}],"tags":["schema","data-protection","static-probe","api-security","authentication","mcp"],"provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-9948-b23539a1495a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"},"initiativeId":"init_01M2GWJNGS4TF5ASSHWGN2004Z"}
