+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5AS0MM2F8MSFTDP36VV9","supersedes":"fnd_01M2GH5AS0MM2F8MSFTDP36VV9","companyId":"example-co","title":"Both Dockerfiles pin node:24-alpine with no content digest","description":"Dockerfile:1 and deploy/aws/Dockerfile:2 both read `FROM node:24-alpine` with no `@sha256:...` digest, so the runtime base of the image behind the order-routing critical function (applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json, eks-prod-mumbai) floats to whatever node:24-alpine currently resolves to at build time. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.MA.S3-mapped applicable control PR.IP.S1 (high). SLA topic: patch-sla.\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (Evidence holds: Dockerfile:1 and deploy/aws/Dockerfile:2 both read `FROM node:24-alpine` with no digest, and no @sha256 pin, base-image build arg or override appears anywhere else in the checkout. The SARIF export has a CICD-PIN-02 fail result at Dockerfile lines 1-1 with maxwell/v1 fingerprint 6c113f0c...5974, the same regulatory refs, invocation executionSuccessful true, revisionId equal to pinnedCommit and the same session and run. details.json links critical function order-routing to mcp-gateway, and prod.json (tier prod, exposure partner, cluster eks-prod-mumbai) points iac at this repo's deploy/ path. Severity high stands, but not for the reason the record gives: catalog PR.DS.S6 applies only to reCategories mii and qualified-re, while example-co is registered as mid-size-re. So the \"catalog defaultSeverity\" basis is doubtful under regulatory-mapping, and high still follows from the SARIF level error under maxwell-conventions section 4 step 3. Two further notes: deploy/aws/README.md describes that Dockerfile as a Bedrock AgentCore image pushed to ECR in us-east-1, so tying it to eks-prod-mumbai is an inference, not something the files state. And the remediation text is wrong in one place: .github/dependabot.yml already has a docker entry, but only for directory \"/\", so deploy/aws/Dockerfile is not covered. (Unverifiable: the export sha256 dc357366... could not be recomputed and no other recorded digest exists to compare it with.)); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The cited clause sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not bind example-co: its catalog applicability is reCategories [mii, qualified-re] and its prose says 'Exempt for Mid-size, Small-size and Self-certification REs', while both of example-co's SEBI registrations are mid-size-re; no sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 control record exists in soc/main.jsonl either, so controlIds would dangle. The mapping is repairable with sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1 (mandatory for all REs, no reCategory limit; its prose requires 'deploying only hardened and vetted hardware and software', which an unpinned floating node:24-alpine base breaks). A control record for it exists in the ledger and its defaultSeverity is high, so severity=high stays correct. SEBI stays first, and nist-ssdf-800-218 (global, empty applicability) stays as a secondary ref next to PR.IP.S1's catalog mapping nist-csf-2.0 PR.PS-01. The description text naming 'PR.DS.S6 (high)' should be updated to match. Note PR.IP.S1's probeWorkflows list does not include probe-cicd-env, but no category-unrestricted CSCRF control that does list it (PR.IP.S4 scanning, PR.MA.S3 patching) covers base-image pinning as directly.).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S1"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-csf-2.0","controlId":"PR.PS-01"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId":"PW.4.4"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"Dockerfile","startLine":1,"endLine":1},"fingerprint":"6c113f0c1e613589795d4adeac167a6eb56c9e169f67c99337b4455f30ff5974","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"CICD-PIN-02","tool":"maxwell-cicd-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","initiativeId":"init_01M2GWK1FRDCWGPJVC10RJS43X","slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T13:48:42Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":[],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/Dockerfile","description":"no-digest FROM"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/deploy/aws/Dockerfile","description":"no-digest FROM"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a/probe-cicd-env.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","description":"CICD-PIN-02 result","sha256":"dc357366ff0f5fbd47e3a1b9e407d5d877f6c5dc16552f0f4c709686ba3c151d"}],"tags":["cicd","supply-chain","static-probe","pinning"],"recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-9948-b23539a1495a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"control","id":"sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1","supersedes":"sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","frameworkRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S1"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-csf-2.0","controlId":"PR.PS-01"},{"regulator":"ISO","instrument":"iso-27001-2022","controlId":"A.8.9"},{"regulator":"CIS","instrument":"cis-controls-8.1","controlId":"4.1"},{"regulator":"CIS","instrument":"cis-controls-8.1","controlId":"4.8"},{"regulator":"CIS","instrument":"cis-controls-8.1","controlId":"2.5"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-800-53-r5","controlId":"CM-2"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-800-53-r5","controlId":"CM-7"}],"title":"Baseline configuration with least functionality; hardening, port whitelisting and application whitelisting","category":"PR.IP","implementationStatus":"planned","effectiveness":"not-tested","nextDueAt":"2026-10-14T09:55:06Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":".claude/skills/regulatory-catalogs/references/catalogs/sebi-cscrf-2024.catalog.json"}],"provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-9948-b23539a1495a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2H0V42KZARY9GX2CKNJYVS4","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1"],"title":"Initiative init_01M2GWK1FRDCWGPJVC10RJS43X raised for 1 finding(s) and 0 risk(s)","description":"Change-management initiative init_01M2GWK1FRDCWGPJVC10RJS43X (type: pin the node:24-alpine base image to a content digest in both mongodb-mcp-server Dockerfiles) was raised, owned by cto@example-co.invalid, due 2026-09-21T21:12:30Z, covering tasks task_1, task_2, task_3, task_4. It remediates finding fnd_01M2GH5AS0MM2F8MSFTDP36VV9 against control sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S1 on applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server.","methods":["impl-change-management"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","result":"not-applicable","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"company-profile/example-co/change_management/master.json"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"company-profile/example-co/change_management/initiatives/init_01M2GWK1FRDCWGPJVC10RJS43X/timeline.json"}],"tags":["change-management","remediation"],"provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-9948-b23539a1495a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5AT8SW3Z6ZTZ73YN7QY6","companyId":"example-co","title":"Unverified binary download in mcp-publish.yml, and deploy/aws/Dockerfile silently ignores its own version pin","description":"mcp-publish.yml:22 runs `curl -L .../mcp-publisher_...tar.gz | tar xz mcp-publisher` with no checksum or signature check, then executes that binary in a job holding `id-token: write` (mcp-publish.yml:11-13) to publish to the MCP registry. Separately, deploy/aws/Dockerfile:3 declares `ARG VERSION=latest` and labels the image `version=${VERSION}`, but deploy/aws/Dockerfile:9 hardcodes `RUN npm install -g mongodb-mcp-server@latest`, ignoring VERSION entirely -- every AWS-image rebuild installs whatever is newest on npm regardless of the version the build was supposedly pinned to. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.IP.S4 (high). SLA topic: patch-sla.\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (The evidence holds, but the control mapping needs repair. mcp-publish.yml:22 really does pipe `curl -L .../latest/download/mcp-publisher_*.tar.gz` into `tar xz`, then runs `./mcp-publisher login github-oidc` and `publish` under `id-token: write`. publish.yml calls it on every new `latest` release. deploy/aws/Dockerfile:3 has `ARG VERSION=latest` and :9 hardcodes `npm install -g mongodb-mcp-server@latest`. The SARIF export has a CICD-PIN-03 fail result with the same fingerprint. sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not apply to example-co (mid-size-re exempt, and no control record exists for it), so the nearest applicable control is PR.IP.S4, which no reCategory filter excludes, lists probe-cicd-env and also defaults to high; severity high stands.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The cited primary clause sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not bind example-co. The fix is sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S4 (\"Scan critical software for malicious code\"), which binds every RE except Small-size and Self-certification, has a ledger control record, and defaultSeverity high, so severity stays high. sebi-cscrf-2024 is correctly first, nist-ssdf-800-218 PW.4.1 is a valid global secondary.)","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S4"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S4"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId":"PW.4.1"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":".github/workflows/mcp-publish.yml","startLine":20,"endLine":22},"fingerprint":"454afe95e14049bfd1a5ae7a9be94a2c724c1e2cb7b8661307bdb1187c0cd007","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"CICD-PIN-03","tool":"maxwell-cicd-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T13:48:42Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":[],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T13:48:42Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/.github/workflows/mcp-publish.yml","description":"unverified curl+tar extraction"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/deploy/aws/Dockerfile","description":"ARG VERSION ignored, hardcoded @latest"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/1a5b055e-58b2-4969-9611-d47c345c064a/probe-cicd-env.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","description":"CICD-PIN-03 result","sha256":"dc357366ff0f5fbd47e3a1b9e407d5d877f6c5dc16552f0f4c709686ba3c151d"}],"tags":["cicd","supply-chain","static-probe","pinning"],"recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-9948-b23539a1495a","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"},"supersedes":"fnd_01M2GH5AT8SW3Z6ZTZ73YN7QY6","initiativeId":"init_0