+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GH5AZ5M0KCRXNTEY3DPH69","companyId":"example-co","title":"Policy's blocking secrets gate (gitleaks) is actually a narrower AWS-only scanner (git-secrets)","description":"company-profile/example-co/sdlc/policy.json ciGates[] declares {gate: secrets, tool: gitleaks, blocking: true, minSeverityToBlock: low}. The only secrets check in the checkout is code-health.yml:193-206 'Run git secrets', which runs `git-secrets --register-aws && git-secrets --scan` -- a different tool that with only --register-aws matches AWS key patterns and does not detect the JIRA/npm/GitHub tokens or MongoDB connection strings this repo's own workflows handle as secrets. Whether the job is a required status check cannot be confirmed because applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server.json has no branchProtection block. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.IP.S4 (high).\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (policy.json declares a secrets gate using gitleaks with blocking true; code-health.yml lines 193-206 run git-secrets --register-aws only; SARIF export has a matching CICD-GATE-06 fail result; no compensating control (.gitleaks.toml, secret_scanning.yml) exists in the checkout.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (PR.IP.S3 is change management and does not cover a secrets-scanning gate; PR.IP.S4's guidance explicitly names secret scanning with blocking gates under probe-cicd-env, has a ledger control record, and shares the high defaultSeverity, so the ref is corrected to PR.IP.S4; iso-27001-2022 A.8.29, nist-ssdf-800-218 PW.7.2 and nist-csf-2.0 PR.PS-06 are taken from PR.IP.S4's catalog mappings.)","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S4"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S4"},{"regulator":"ISO","instrument":"iso-27001-2022","controlId":"A.8.29"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId