+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GSDSE000HR9FYWXXSM4ZM3","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"vitest coverage runs in CI but no minimum coverage threshold is configured anywhere","description":"policy.json ciGates[] declares {gate: unit-tests, tool: vitest, blocking: true} with no threshold field. code-health.yml run-tests job executes `pnpm test` (vitest --coverage --run) on push to main and same-repo pull_request events and the coverage job merges and uploads lcov to Coveralls, but vitest.config.ts coverage block (lines 30-44) sets only exclude and reporter: [lcov] -- no thresholds/lines/branches/statements minimum. No .nycrc, codecov.yml or comparable fail_under configuration exists elsewhere in the checkout.\n\nImpact: A pull request that drops test coverage on write-capable MongoDB/Atlas tool code cannot fail the unit-tests gate on that basis; the only enforcement is that existing tests keep passing, not that new code is exercised.\n\nRemediation: Add vitest coverage.thresholds (lines/branches/statements/functions) to vitest.config.ts, or a codecov.yml target, and make the coverage job (code-health.yml) fail the build when the threshold is not met; add it to branchProtection.statusChecks.","severity":"medium","confidence":"possible","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S6"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S6"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-ssdf-800-218","controlId":"PW.8.2"},{"regulator":"ISO","instrument":"iso-27001-2022","controlId":"A.8.29"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"vitest.config.ts","startLine":30,"endLine":44},"fingerprint":"7b28ad9bb3c053384d1fe7a3325f28d9a49a5b3a7ae170a36312672e49b5149b","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"ssdf-pw-8-2-no-coverage-threshold","tool":"maxwell-sdlc-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","initiativeId":"init_01M2GWJR746MQDJ90VX