+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GJYP56VKDHARQPPFVATT0D","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"AWS Bedrock AgentCore Dockerfile has no pinned base image or package version","description":"deploy/aws/Dockerfile line 2 (`FROM node:24-alpine`) carries no digest, line 3 (`ARG VERSION=latest`) is only used to stamp a LABEL and does not pin anything actually installed, and line 9 (`RUN npm install -g mongodb-mcp-server@latest`) installs whatever the latest published mongodb-mcp-server release is at build time with no lockfile. This image is the one deploy/aws/README.md instructs operators to build and push to ECR for the AgentCore runtime; the checkout has no image records under applications/mcp-gateway/images linking it to qa/prod, which run on EKS ap-south-1. This is inconsistent with company-profile/example-co/sdlc/policy.json dependencyPolicy.lockfilesRequired = true, and it means two builds on different days can silently ship different, unreviewed code. Severity is the sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.IP.S3 catalog defaultSeverity (sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not apply: example-co is registered mid-size-re and that control's applicability is limited to mii, qualified-re). SLA topic: patch-sla. Commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (The cited evidence holds but the record overstates two things, both fixable: deploy/aws/Dockerfile really does have `FROM node:24-alpine` with no digest (line 2), `ARG VERSION=latest` used only for a LABEL (lines 3 and 24) and `RUN npm install -g mongodb-mcp-server@latest` (line 9); nothing in the checkout references deploy/aws or overrides it with a build-arg; and the SARIF export has an IAC-DRIFT-01 fail result at deploy/aws/Dockerfile lines 2-9 with maxwell/v1 fingerprint 99dd6cfe...be4d, the same refs, executionSuccessful true, revisionId equal to pinnedCommit and this session and run. First problem, the severity basis: sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.DS.S6 applies only to reCategories [mii, qualified-re], its prose says 'Exempt for Mid-size, Small-size and Self-certification REs', both example-co SEBI registrations are mid-size-re, and the ledger has no sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 control record, so controlIds would dangle; the ledger already applied the fix to fnd_01M2GH5AS0MM2F8MSFTDP36VV9, citing PR.IP.S1 (control record at main.jsonl line 76, mandatory, no reCategory limit, defaultSeverity high), so high stays. Second problem, deployment: nothing shows this AgentCore image is deployed; qa/prod run on EKS ap-south-1 (env JSONs, app README), deploy/aws/README.md pushes to ECR us-east-1 for Bedrock AgentCore, there are no image records under applications/mcp-gateway/images, and the only link is env iac[].path 'deploy', so the 'serving the same pii/financial stores' and 'production data path' wording must be softened. Also, the unpinned base image on deploy/aws/Dockerfile:2 is already recorded in open finding fnd_01M2GH5AS0MM2F8MSFTDP36VV9 (CICD-PIN-02), so only the `@latest` npm install is new here. (unverifiable: SARIF sha256 5b29e0ed... cannot be recomputed and no other recorded digest for that path exists)); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The finding stands, but its main SEBI clause is wrong and needs fixing. sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S6 does not apply to example-co: the catalog limits it to mii and qualified-re (\"Exempt for Mid-size, Small-size and Self-certification REs\"), both of example-co's SEBI registrations are mid-size-re, the ledger has no control record for PR.DS.S6, and probe-iac is not one of its probe workflows. Earlier refuter verdicts in the ledger (lines 701 and 706) already said the same. The fix is sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S3 (configuration change control and change management). It covers mii, qualified-re and mid-size-re, lists probe-iac with guidance on infrastructure drift outside the pipeline, has a control record at ledger line 78, and has defaultSeverity high, so severity stays high. Crosswalks should come from PR.IP.S3's catalog mappings: nist-ssdf PS.2.1 and ISO A.8.30 are only PR.DS.S6 mappings, and A.8.30 (outsourced development) does not fit this gap. SEBI is correctly listed first, and sebi-cscrf-2024, iso-27001-2022 and nist-ssdf-800-218 all apply to example-co. The Dockerfile lines 2, 3 and 9 match the description. I did not check the patch-sla topic or the SLA, because the ledger keeper computes slaBasis later; I also did not open the SARIF export, because this lens does not need it.).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.IP.S3"},{"regulator":"ISO","instrument":"iso-27001-2022","controlId":"A.8.32"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-csf-2.0","controlId":"PR.PS-01"},{"regulator":"CIS","instrument":"cis-controls-8.1","controlId":"4.2"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"deploy/aws/Dockerfile","startLine":2,"endLine":9},"fingerprint":"99dd6cfed47baeff1e52bfb0beac191df32ba69eb42096880ff655464d8fbe4d","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"IAC-DRIFT-01","tool":"maxwell-iac-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","initiativeId":"init_01M2GWQ198WX455NVQVAQ62EST","slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T18:08:50Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:08:50Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:08:50Z","evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/ba28bc2c-2822-41eb-92a8-b6389d3f1d0d/probe-iac.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","description":"IAC-DRIFT-01 result","sha256":"5b29e0ed1bfa28809f81d34e55648dda20c31112a65dd894f8ecf5bf4f03f7bb"}],"tags":["iac","static-probe","supply-chain","hygiene"],"supersedes":"fnd_01M2GJYP56VKDHARQPPFVATT0D","provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","sessionId":"01b78802-3bc9-4e5c-99