+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GMN63DEDR29P66QTKND8E7","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:12:30Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"No retention, expiry or purge mechanism for personal data or trading credentials","description":"Neither class User(Document) (models.py:387-429) nor class Secrets(Document) (8-15) declares an expires_at/retention_until field, a TTL index in `meta`, or even an is_active/deleted_at soft-delete flag - the only date fields are account_creation_date and the crypto/equity integration timestamps, none of which are a retention control. There is no purge path anywhere in this 4-file checkout for personal data or connected-broker credentials once their purpose ends or consent is withdrawn. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S13. SLA topic: data-retention. dpdp-rules-2025 8(1) (Third Schedule inactivity erasure) binds only e-commerce, online gaming and social media fiduciaries above user thresholds and does not apply to this broker/DP/NBFC, so the DPDP Act 8(7) retention-limitation duty is cited instead, alongside dpdp-act-2023:8(7). Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (User and Secrets confirmed to have no expires_at, retention_until, TTL meta or soft-delete field; no purge path in the 4-file checkout; neither metastore.json nor policy.json records retention for these collections; SARIF SCH-RET-02 fail result matches at the same path and lines 387-429 with the same fingerprint; medium matches the catalog defaultSeverity of PR.AA.S13). regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S13, retention and disposal policy with purge jobs, cited first for a SEBI mid-size RE; dpdp-rules-2025:8(1) does not bind this entity type so it is replaced with the DPDP Act 8(7) retention-limitation duty and its Rules cross-reference Act-8(7); owasp-asvs-5.0 14.2.7 is a global crosswalk, wording unverified offline).","severity":"medium","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S13","dpdp